# Procedures example: domain profile [PROFILE:PROCEDURES-EXAMPLE-PROFILE]

> Found by directory auto-discovery: lint looks for a `*-profile.lts` file in the corpus root, so this file needs no registry entry. Its rules run only because it is in scope; a corpus with no profile in scope reports its profile-driven rules as inert.

## [PROFILE-DOMAIN] Domain identity

- domain-id: example.procedures
- domain-name: Procedures example
- domain-version: 1

## Registered node-id prefixes

### [PREFIX-PROC] PROC

- registers-prefix: PROC-
- definition: a procedure, the root of a set of steps

### [PREFIX-STEP] STEP

- registers-prefix: STEP-
- definition: one step of a procedure

### [PREFIX-DEC] DEC

- registers-prefix: DEC-
- definition: a decision a procedure implements

### [PREFIX-INV] INV

- registers-prefix: INV-
- definition: an invariant a procedure keeps

### [PREFIX-MATRIX] MATRIX

- registers-prefix: MATRIX-
- definition: a decision matrix that chooses between procedures

### [PREFIX-DOC] DOC

- registers-prefix: DOC-
- definition: a document's root node

## Status values

### [ENUM-STATUS] Status

- enum-key: status
- values:
  - draft
  - active
  - retired

## Required and recommended properties

### [NODEFAMILY-PROC] PROC nodes

- section: procedures
- families: PROC-
- required:
  - trigger
  - owner
  - status
- recommended:
  - must-not
  - last-reviewed

### [NODEFAMILY-STEP] STEP nodes

- section: steps
- families: STEP-
- required:
  - actor
  - action

## Declared property keys

A document stamped `lts: "1.1"` treats an undeclared key as a lint ERROR. That includes this profile's own structural keys, so they are declared first.

